    value={ "title": "3-07. Cleaning Frequency [A]", "description": """This field defines which cleaning frequencies are available and which are not. The Agent uses it to
present valid scheduling options during cleaning estimate conversations.

**Important:** Enter this value as a list. Cleaning prompts inject this text directly, so free-form
paragraphs can make the available options unclear.

**Best Practice:** Separate the list into offering vs not offering sections so the Agent can guide
customers without ambiguity.

**Examples:**

```txt
- **Offering:**
  - One-time cleaning (OTC): \"Our One-time only cleans are normally $75 per hour per person, and our office has a 2-hour minimum for $300.\"
  - Weekly
  - Every 2 Weeks or BiWeekly
  - Every 4 Weeks
- **Not Offering:**
  - Monthly: not offering, but may relay a message to the manager for a special request.
  - Every 3 Weeks
  - Other options
```

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** Inserted into the reusable cleaning-frequency procedure and the cleaning
approximate-estimate scenario so the Agent only offers the schedule options listed here when asking
the customer to choose a cleaning frequency.

**Fallbacks:** On first initialization, this field can be populated from Agent Creator cleaning
intake. If it is blank, the cleaning prompts that display frequency choices do not receive a
predefined list of options.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - None. This attribute does not require another customer-facing setting before it can be
    initialized or used.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `agent_creator_cleaning_frequency`: First-init source for this attribute.
  - `project_attributes_setting_products_and_services_background_check_location_enabled`: Advanced
    system configuration that changes whether service-area verification happens before the Agent
    reaches the cleaning-frequency step in the approximate-estimate scenario.""", "group": "3. Knowledge Base", "value_type": "string", "is_hidden": False }
)}}

