{# #### `project_attributes_cleaning_appointment_url` #}

{{SetCustomerMetadataAttribute(
    idn="project_attributes_cleaning_appointment_url",
    field="multiple_fields",
    value={ "title": "4-20. Cleaning Appointment Link (URL) [A] [IMPORTANT]", "description": """Set the URL where users can book a cleaning appointment online.

**Best Practice:** Use a direct scheduling page URL, not a generic homepage, so the Agent can share
a clear next step.

**Examples:**

- `https://booking.yourcleaningbrand.com/appointment`
- `https://yourcleaningbrand.com/book-cleaning`

---

**⚙️ Technical & System Details (Advanced)**

**System Usage:** Copied into the cleaning business context and tech variables, and included in the
default cleaning send-information content for SMS and optional email as the `[appointment_url]`
placeholder.

**Fallbacks:** On first initialization, this can be copied from
`agent_creator_cleaning_appointment_url`. If it remains empty, the default cleaning send-information
content still includes the `[appointment_url]` placeholder until you provide a real booking link or
customize the template.

**Dependencies:**

- **Primary Settings:**
  - None. This attribute does not require another customer-facing setting before it can be
    initialized or used.
- **Logic Interactions:**
  - `agent_creator_cleaning_appointment_url`: First-init source for this attribute.
  - `project_attributes_cleaning_estimate_url`: Cleaning business context and default
    send-information content expose estimate and appointment links together, so both are commonly
    available during quote-to-book handoffs.
  - `project_attributes_setting_sms_send_information_allowed_content`: Cleaning SMS templates
    include appointment-link content that uses this value.
  - `project_attributes_setting_email_send_information_allowed_content`: Cleaning email templates
    include appointment-link content that uses this value when email sending is enabled.""", "group": "4. Agent Behavior", "value_type": "string", "is_hidden": False }
)}}

